triage: fix_game: In all four failing scenarios the scripted bids never reached the game. The report says the bid options (0, 2, 3, 22) were never put to the seats, and every recorded bid was 0, so the active player won every all-zero tie. The tests' expectations are consistent with the rules once their bids are applied, so the bid step in the file is at fault.
step C: building the game file
triage: fix_game: Both recurring failures are mistakes in the game file, not limits of the rules or the platform. Prompts interpolate names the step cannot fill ({offer}, {church_count}), and the offer is shown while the public lot and gift are still ''. The attempts swing between these two faults because each fix reintroduced the other.

